                <pb facs="0113" n="29" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg29"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72114/3567</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-05-01T13:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 1, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1564. Department’s 1127, March 22, 3 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d47-f1"/>
                    Translation of Foreign Office note received today states: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>The treatment for American citizens incorporated in the Royal Army who
                            may be captured by the enemy will be completely the same as that of
                            Italian prisoners of war. The Royal Government will provide for their
                            clothing and food in the measure adopted for Italian prisoners of war,
                            and in case of officers, will cause them to receive their pay in the
                            same manner as is practiced for Italian officer prisoners, to be
                            reimbursed at the end of the war. Finally, parcels of food can freely be
                            sent to American prisoners of war through the American Red Cross from
                            the stocks which this organization has at its disposal in
                            Switzerland.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
